<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20995" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hortŭlus</span></b> , i, m.
		dim.
		hortus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a little garden.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Cat. 61,
			92</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 3, 226</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 35,
				10, 36, § 105</span></i>; as <i>part of a
				vineyard</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 4, 18, 2</span></i>.—In
				plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hortuli,</span>”
				<i>garden-grounds</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Off. 3, 14, 58</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Fin. 5, 1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Clu. 13,
				37</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 4, 18,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: Cupidinis, i. e. pudenda muliebria,
			App. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀνεχ</span>.
			17.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cujus (Democriti) fontibus Epicurus hortulos
					suos irrigavit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 1, 43, 120</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
